                                                   This in particular confirms a conjecture of Leonida and Li.




                                                                                     1. Introduction
                                             Throughout, all graphs are finite, simple, and undirected. For a graph G of order n, let
                                           A(G) denote its adjacency matrix and let
                                                                                    λ1 (G) ≥ · · · ≥ λn (G)
                                           be the eigenvalues of A(G). Order-only bounds for adjacency eigenvalues have a long
                                           history; see, for example, Hong [1, 2], Powers [9], and Nikiforov [8].
                                              In [9], Powers proposed, for connected graphs, the order-only bound
                                                                                     jnk
                                                                           λi (G) ≤           (1 ≤ i ≤ n/2).
                                                                                       i
                                           As pointed out later by Nikiforov [8], the original proof is flawed. Nevertheless, the bound
                                           is valid for i ≤ 2: the case i = 1 is trivial, and Hong proved the stronger estimate λ2 (G) ≤
                                           (n − 2)/2 for every graph of order n [1]. By contrast, Nikiforov’s constructions show
                                           that Powers’s bound fails for every i ≥ 5 [8], while Linz [6] ruled out the case i = 4 by
                                           constructing graphs with λ4 (G) > n/4. Since connectivity plays no role for i = 3, the
                                           only remaining positive case may be stated as follows; see also [7, Problem 10] and [8,
                                           Question 2.11].
                                           Problem 1.1 (Nikiforov [8]). Let G be a graph of order n ≥ 3. Is it true that
                                                                                            jnk
                                                                                   λ3 (G) ≤     ?
                                                                                             3
                                              Recently, Leonida and Li [4, Theorem 1.6] verified Problem 1.1 for several important
                                           classes of graphs, including strongly regular graphs, regular line graphs, and Cayley graphs

                                             2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. Primary 05C50; Secondary 15A18, 15A42.
                                             Key words and phrases. adjacency eigenvalues, third eigenvalue, spectral graph theory, symmetric
